SLUG: services/loading-unloading.html
TITLE: Loading & Unloading in Kanpur — labour only
DESC: Trained crews in Kanpur for loading and unloading when you have your own vehicle or have packed yourself. Trolleys and straps, stairs and no-lift buildings planned for.
HEADING: Loading &amp; unloading
LEAD: Labour only, for when you have your own vehicle or have already packed. The lifting is the part most people underestimate.
CRUMBS: Home|/ ; Services|/services.html ; Loading &amp; unloading|
---

  <section class="section on-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split is-wide-left">
        <div>
          <h2>Loading is a skill, not just strength</h2>
          <p class="lead">
            A badly loaded vehicle damages goods even on a smooth road,
            because everything inside is free to move. A well-loaded one holds
            itself still.
          </p>
          <p>
            Heavy and flat items go in first and low, against the walls.
            Fragile cartons ride on top, never underneath. Gaps are filled so
            nothing can slide, and the load is strapped in sections rather
            than as one mass — so if one strap loosens, the whole load does
            not shift.
          </p>
          <p>
            We sign off a loading sheet with you before the vehicle moves, so
            both sides know exactly what went on.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <span class="card__icon"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-lift"/></svg></span>
          <h3>What the crew brings</h3>
          <ul class="ticks">
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Trolleys and sack barrows for cartons and appliances</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Lifting straps for wardrobes, sofas and double-door fridges</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Floor and door-frame protection on the carry route</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Ratchet straps and blankets for securing the load</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Basic tools for beds and table legs that must come off to fit</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section on-sunk">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Planning</span>
        <h2>Tell us these three things and the quote will be right</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>The floor, and whether the lift works</h3>
          <p>
            A fourth floor without a lift is not "a bit harder" — it needs
            more people to do safely in the same time. This is the single
            biggest factor in a labour-only quote.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>How far the vehicle can park</h3>
          <p>
            Carry distance is invisible on a phone call and obvious at 8am.
            Fifty metres each way, repeated for every item, is an hour of
            work nobody priced.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>The awkward items</h3>
          <p>
            A double-door fridge, a three-seater that will not turn on the
            landing, a glass table top, a treadmill. Each may need extra
            hands or a different route out.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section on-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="wrap-narrow">
        <h2>Questions we get asked</h2>
        <div class="faq mt-6" data-faq>
          <details>
            <summary>Can I hire just the crew, with my own vehicle?</summary>
            <div class="faq__body"><p>
              Yes. That is exactly what this service is. We will still advise
              on whether your vehicle is the right size, because a second trip
              costs more than the right truck would have.
            </p></div>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Will you move things I packed myself?</summary>
            <div class="faq__body"><p>
              Yes. Note that owner-packed cartons are normally outside transit
              cover, since nobody can verify the contents or the packing — so
              pack sturdy items yourself and consider having the fragile ones
              professionally packed.
            </p></div>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>How many people will come?</summary>
            <div class="faq__body"><p>
              It depends on the volume, the floor and the lift. We state the
              crew size in the quote rather than sending "a team" and deciding
              on the day.
            </p></div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- Photographs of real jobs. Generated by
       tools/gallery/add-photo-strips.ps1 -- edit the mapping there, not
       here, or the next run will not know this strip exists. -->
  <section class="section is-tight on-sunk" aria-labelledby="shots-service-loading-unloading" data-photo-strip>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">From our own jobs</span>
        <h2 id="shots-service-loading-unloading">Carrying and loading</h2>
        <p class="lead">Heavy flat items carried by hand through doorways, stacked goods moved on a trolley.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="workshots">
        <figure class="workshot">
          <img class="workshot__img"
               src="/assets/images/gallery/crew-moving-wrapped-panel-400.jpg"
               srcset="/assets/images/gallery/crew-moving-wrapped-panel-400.jpg 400w, /assets/images/gallery/crew-moving-wrapped-panel-1000.jpg 1000w"
               sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 22rem, (min-width: 40rem) 45vw, 92vw"
               alt="A crew member carrying a large wrapped flat item through a doorway."
               width="301" height="400" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        </figure>
        <figure class="workshot">
          <img class="workshot__img"
               src="/assets/images/gallery/strapped-cartons-on-trolley-400.jpg"
               srcset="/assets/images/gallery/strapped-cartons-on-trolley-400.jpg 400w, /assets/images/gallery/strapped-cartons-on-trolley-1000.jpg 1000w"
               sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 22rem, (min-width: 40rem) 45vw, 92vw"
               alt="Cartons strapped in stacks on a flat trolley outside a building."
               width="400" height="301" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          <figcaption class="workshot__cap">Strapped in stacks, moved on a trolley</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="workshot">
          <img class="workshot__img"
               src="/assets/images/gallery/crew-with-wrapped-panels-400.jpg"
               srcset="/assets/images/gallery/crew-with-wrapped-panels-400.jpg 400w, /assets/images/gallery/crew-with-wrapped-panels-1000.jpg 1000w"
               sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 22rem, (min-width: 40rem) 45vw, 92vw"
               alt="A crew member beside several tall wrapped panels lined up indoors."
               width="301" height="400" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        </figure>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6"><a class="link-cta" href="/gallery.html">
        All 44 photographs
        <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow-right"/></svg>
      </a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section is-tight cta-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="wrap-narrow text-centre">
        <h2>Need hands, not a whole move?</h2>
        <p class="lead">Tell us the floor, the lift and the awkward items, and we will quote the labour.</p>
        <div class="btn-row mt-6 btn-row--centre">
          <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/contact.html" data-open-callback>Request a callback</a>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/services.html">All services</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
